  "goodToKnow": "Das Aquarell is a watercolour painting, and die Aquarellmalerei the technique. Albrecht Dürer's watercolour landscapes from around 1495, painted on his journey to Italy, are among the earliest in European art; his famous Feldhase (young hare, 1502) combines watercolour and gouache and is in Vienna's Albertina. Plural: die Aquarelle."
